 "news": {
  "date": "2026-10-27",
  "asof": "2026-10-28 10:57 UTC",
  "headline": "A rally on financing, flat yields, crude under $100 \u2014 and today the Fed and Alphabet share an hour",
  "standfirst": "The AI rally ran a second day on money rather than demand: Wall Street banks and Blackstone arranged $63bn so Anthropic can buy Broadcom's AI chips, Broadcom rose about 3.8%, and the Nasdaq gained 1.18% with the Russell up 1.16% and the semiconductor index back above 11,300. The S&P rose 0.60% but most of its members fell, and the Dow added just 15.99 points as Boeing missed with a $0.34 core loss. Consumer confidence rose to 91.7 against 80.4 expected; UPS and Coca-Cola beat and raised. Yields barely moved as the Fed's two-day meeting began \u2014 two-year 4.735%, ten-year 4.99%, thirty-year 5.30% \u2014 with about 83% priced for a December increase. WTI settled $99.90, back below $100, and Brent $113.88 as peace talks drew attention; gold rose 1.08% to $4,060.20. In the book GOOG rose 0.84% to 316.83, its first gain since 19 October after five lower closes, to -0.45R. The day +2.64; Q4 +25.61 with +34.64 realised. Heat 1.01R, 1.99R spare. The Fed and Alphabet report today.",
  "themes": [
   {
    "kicker": "What's next",
    "right": "the Fed and Alphabet today",
    "title": "Today, then PCE and Amazon tomorrow",
    "items": [
     {
      "tone": "c-fomc",
      "tag": "FOMC \u00b7 GOOG",
      "html": "<b>Fed decision and Alphabet Q3 in the same hour</b> \u2014 a hold is close to certain; Alphabet brings $195-205bn of capex and a $3.00 consensus",
      "when": "Wed \u00b7 2026-10-28",
      "kind": "calendar"
     },
     {
      "tone": "c-cb",
      "tag": "PCE \u00b7 AMZN",
      "html": "<b>September PCE and Amazon Q3</b> \u2014 the inflation measure the Fed targets, and the next hyperscaler to account for its spending",
      "when": "Thu \u00b7 2026-10-29",
      "kind": "calendar"
     },
     {
      "tone": "c-er",
      "tag": "AAPL",
      "html": "<b>iPhone Duo in 28 more countries</b> \u2014 the second wave, with display-crack reports circulating",
      "when": "Fri \u00b7 2026-10-30",
      "kind": "calendar"
     },
     {
      "tone": "c-cb",
      "tag": "EARNINGS",
      "html": "<b>Apple Q4 and Palantir Q3</b> \u2014 both out of this book, read for the consumer and the software cycle",
      "when": "Mon \u00b7 2026-11-02",
      "kind": "calendar"
     },
     {
      "tone": "c-fomc",
      "tag": "VOTE",
      "html": "<b>US midterms</b> \u2014 the date the reported Iran strike plans sit behind",
      "when": "Tue \u00b7 2026-11-03",
      "kind": "calendar"
     }
    ],
    "note": "<b>Today: the statement, not the decision.</b> A hold is close to certain and CME futures put about <b>83% on a December increase</b>. What matters is whether the Fed describes the energy shock as an inflation risk or a growth risk \u2014 the market has argued it both ways inside a week, and Tuesday's <b>91.7 consumer confidence</b> hands the inflation side a fresh argument. In the same hour <b>Alphabet reports $195-205bn of capex against a consensus near $3.00</b>, with its chief executive on record that cloud revenue is being deferred."
   }
  ],
